<title>GERMANY: Munich Re plans dividend rise for 96/97 yr.</title>
<headline>Munich Re plans dividend rise for 96/97 yr.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Business year to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		  just under 700     vs 595</p>
<p>    Group DVFA earnings per share		150     vs 140</p>
<p>    Group sales				   32,000  up 10 pct</p>
<p>    Group underwriting profit		    800     vs 573</p>
<p>    Group capital investments		147,000  up 27,000</p>
<p>    Group profit from investments	    9,300   vs 7,900</p>
<p>    Proposed dividend			    17 dm   vs 16 dm</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurance group is Muenchener Rueckversicherungs- AG, or Munich Re. The insurer said the results for 1996/1997 given above are approximate. The underwriting profit is calculated before changes in the claims equalisation reserve. Final results for 1996/1997 will be discussed at a supervisory board meeting on October 23.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
